latest_plan = 'Based on the reflection, here\'s a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Parse the input grid:\n   a. Determine the dimensions of the input grid.\n   b. Identify the midpoints to divide the grid into four quadrants.\n\n2. Process each quadrant:\n   a. Extract the subgrid for each quadrant.\n   b. Identify all red (2) cells in the quadrant.\n   c. If the number of red cells is 0, set the corresponding 3x3 output area to all black.\n   d. If the red cells fit within a 3x3 area, transfer the pattern directly.\n   e. If the pattern is larger than 3x3:\n      - Calculate the "center of mass" of red cells.\n      - Divide the quadrant into a 3x3 grid.\n      - For each cell in this 3x3 grid:\n        * Check if there are any red cells in the corresponding area of the original quadrant.\n        * If yes, set this cell to red (2).\n        * If multiple areas have red cells, prioritize the one closest to the center of mass.\n   f. Ensure at least one red cell in the 3x3 output if the original quadrant had any red cells.\n\n3. Create the 7x7 output grid:\n   a. Initialize a 7x7 grid with all black (0) cells.\n   b. Place the processed 3x3 patterns from each quadrant into the corners of the 7x7 grid.\n   c. Set row 4 to all black, separating the top and bottom halves.\n\n4. Process the middle column (column 4):\n   a. For rows 0-2 and 5-7:\n      - If there are red cells in both columns 3 and 5 of the same row, set the cell in column 4 to red.\n      - If there are red cells in column 3 or 5 of the adjacent rows, consider setting the cell in column 4 to red to maintain vertical connectivity.\n   b. Keep row 4 black to maintain separation.\n\n5. Final adjustments:\n   a. Scan the entire 7x7 grid to ensure that if a quadrant had any red cells, its corresponding 3x3 area in the output has at least one red cell.\n   b. Check for any isolated red cells and consider removing them if they don\'t contribute to the overall pattern or connectivity.\n\n6. Validate the output:\n   a. Ensure the grid is 7x7.\n   b. Verify that only values 0 (black) and 2 (red) are used.\n   c. Confirm that row 4 is entirely black.\n\n7. Return the final 7x7 ColoredGrid object.\n\nThis plan addresses the key aspects of pattern extraction, simplification of larger patterns, handling of sparse patterns, and connectivity between quadrants. It also includes steps to ensure minimum representation and final validation, which should help in creating a more robust and accurate solution for all possible input cases.'
